msgid "Duchess of the Night"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Duke of the Night, race=deep, gender=male,female
#: Deep/units/Dukeofthenight.cfg:27
msgid "Long ago there was a forest-bound kingdom of many different kin, with its lord and lady known as fierce defenders of the land. But through war it was sullied, and although its invaders withdrew, many lives were lost. Now the forests are void and dark, and at night, one must be careful not to encounter vengeful specters from the past."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Deep/units/Dukeofthenight.cfg:107
msgid "greatsword"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: Deep/units/Dukeofthenight.cfg:116
msgid "prey"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Emissary, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Emissary.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Emissary"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Emissary, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Emissary.cfg:21
msgid "Elite messengers become the quick emissaries of powerful leaders, whom they gained the trust of after decades of work. Swift as the wind, they are matched in speed only by the griffins of the high peaks. As they often carry messages of high importance in troubled times, they can defend themselves quite well by using their sharp talons and unrivalled air mobility. "
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: Deep/units/Emissary.cfg:113
#: Deep/units/Messenger.cfg:108
#: Deep/units/Traveller.cfg:104
msgid "sky dive"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Enchantress, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Enchantress.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Enchantress"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Enchantress, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Enchantress.cfg:21
msgid "The legendary deep enchantresses are beings admired by the majority of people. They carry themselves with grace and confidence, knowing full well the power they hold over the ordinary folk. Thanks to their influence, they develop a network of connections to support their own goals or those they are given by deep lorekeepers."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Endsinger Deep, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Endsinger.cfg:4
msgid "Endsinger Deep"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Endsinger Deep, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Endsinger.cfg:21
msgid "It is said Deep lived forever in their island of mists. But as they left it to gain true flesh and blood, their everlasting youth was lost, and some sought to reclaim it."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=fire
#: Deep/units/Endsinger.cfg:102
msgid "song of extinction"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: Deep/units/Endsinger.cfg:115
msgid "soul drain"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Falconeer, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Falconeer.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Falconeer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Falconeer, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Falconeer.cfg:20
msgid "Various birds are popular among Deep as pets. Among them, falcons are used for hunting, and warfare when the need arises. Some Deep can easily mimic their calls, granting the bird and its wielder excellent coordination. "
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Deep/units/Falconeer.cfg:104
#: Deep/units/Featherlord.cfg:126
#: Deep/units/Flagbearer.cfg:120
msgid "falcon"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Featherlord, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Featherlord.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Featherlord"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Featherlord, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Featherlord.cfg:21
msgid "Deep commanders use their bird companion and specific calls to quickly transmit orders on the battlefield. Their brightly colored flag helps them catch their allies' attention to redirect troops wherever necessary. "
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Deep/units/Featherlord.cfg:116
#: Deep/units/Flagbearer.cfg:110
#: Deep/units/Raider.cfg:61
#: Deep/units/Raider.cfg:71
msgid "lance"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Fighter, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Fighter.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Fighter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Fighter, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Fighter.cfg:20
msgid "Deep can already cause harm with their sharp talons. However, those tasked to fight the colony's foes often reinforce their claws with small blades. Their light gambeson allows them to resist hits slightly better while retaining their kind's mobility. "
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Flagbearer, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Flagbearer.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Flagbearer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Flagbearer, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Flagbearer.cfg:20
msgid "The habit of guiding their bird around gives Deep skills in observing and giving out orders, which are applicable in wide scale combat as well. Some falconeers take up the flag-bearing spear to lead their peers in battle, and while their fighting strength is lesser than others', the coordination they bring to the squadron makes it much more deadly. "
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Flockmaster, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Flockmaster.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Flockmaster"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Flockmaster, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Flockmaster.cfg:21
msgid "Deep whose love for birds is extreme spend their life with them, flying and hunting together. With their skilled calls they bring together small flocks of hawks to help them, directing them to reach their goal more efficiently. "
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Deep/units/Flockmaster.cfg:45
#: Deep/units/Raptortongue.cfg:41
msgid "falcon storm"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Galesinger, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Galesinger.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Galesinger"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Galesinger, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Galesinger.cfg:19
msgid "Experienced minstrels may decide to become the keepers of deep knowledge. They spend years learning from their masters the thousands of songs that relate deep lore. Among these chants are magic spells that allow them to bend the winds to their will, that Deep have used since olden times to travel across the ocean. "
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Deep/units/Galesinger.cfg:57
#: Deep/units/Nightdeep.cfg:108
#: Deep/units/Shrieker.cfg:108
#: Deep/units/Songstressofstorms.cfg:58
#: Deep/units/Stalkerwing.cfg:109
msgid "claws"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=cold
#: Deep/units/Galesinger.cfg:66
#: Deep/units/Songstressofstorms.cfg:67
msgid "Song of gale"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Messenger, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Messenger.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Messenger"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Messenger, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Messenger.cfg:20
msgid "Due to their numerous travels, deep wanderers end up mingling with other races a lot more. Often they will offer their service as long range messengers to various folk. The time spent hunting in the wild has given them keen eyes which serve them well in battle also. "
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Minstrel, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Minstrel.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Minstrel"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Minstrel, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Minstrel.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Deep avoid other races whenever possible, and are seldom welcomed warmly. There is however an exception : minstrels are renowned for their incredible singing. Some say their voice can make anyone fall in awe and completely forget their surroundings. Although the public usually admires their talent, people sometimes fear their supposed powers.\n"
"They wander between towns, living off their art or flying away quickly when they feel threatened. Some of them end up settling down in human cities, but more often than not they keep traveling and act as informants for deep communities."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: Deep/units/Minstrel.cfg:102
#: Deep/units/Siren.cfg:158
msgid "beguiling song"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Nightgaunt, race=deep, gender=female,male
#: Deep/units/Nightgaunt.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Phantom"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Nightgaunt, race=deep, gender=female,male
#: Deep/units/Nightgaunt.cfg:26
msgid ""
"When the night is at its darkest, are the shadows not more enticing than ever? Hide in the night, enjoy it, use it, but never forget it is not your friend. Those that fear not the shadows will in time join their ranks.\n"
"-Tales of the owl hunters"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Deep/units/Nightgaunt.cfg:71
msgid "deathclaws"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Night Deep, race=deep, gender=female,male
#: Deep/units/Nightdeep.cfg:4
msgid "Night Deep"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Night Deep, race=deep, gender=female,male
#: Deep/units/Nightdeep.cfg:28
msgid "While most Deep prefer to build their homes in the caves dotting seashore cliffs and tall mountains, some have chosen to seek shelter in forests. This new environment has made them change their hunting techniques, which now rely on stealth a lot more. Over time their body evolved and they can now fly silently, which makes them extremely hard to notice at night. "
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Parader, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Parader.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Parader"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Parader, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Parader.cfg:20
msgid "As they better their magical craft, some minstrels take delight in catching other's eyes. Switching focus from songs to dance, their plumage changes to reflect their spell-weaving. Paraders, on the opposite of captivators, mean to be noticed, and distract their foes to give their allies more opportunities. "
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Pirate, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Pirate.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Pirate"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Pirate, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Pirate.cfg:20
msgid "Oftentimes deep warriors band together to attack trade ships. They use long pikes to attack in a safer way and stay out of reach of melee fighters with their wings. Pirate groups nest on isolated craggy islands where they store their loot before trading it with other deep colonies. "
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: Deep/units/Pirate.cfg:59
#: Deep/units/Pirate.cfg:69
msgid "spear"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Raider, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Raider.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Raider"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Raider, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Raider.cfg:21
msgid "The seasoned deep soldiers often come from former bandit crews. They lend their talent as mercenaries to various armed forces, who make good use of their ability to strike anywhere quickly. "
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Raptortongue, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Raptortongue.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Raptortongue"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Raptortongue, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Raptortongue.cfg:20
msgid "Over time falconeers efficiently learn the falcons' language. As the bird ages their tamer often will bring in new recruits for taming. "
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Resplendent Deep, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Resplendent.cfg:4
msgid "Resplendent Deep"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Resplendent Deep, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Resplendent.cfg:22
msgid ""
"Resplendent Deep make the most of their dazzling presence to help their allies go unnoticed. In social gatherings where they thrive, they know when to show glitter and when to lay low so as not to displease their host.\n"
"In battle they learnt to be very nimble, avoiding the harm that comes with being the center of attention, and confuse the enemy by making their presence clear or hidden to be harder to catch. "
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Rockthrower, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Rockthrower.cfg:4
msgid "Deep Rockthrower"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Rockthrower, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Rockthrower.cfg:20
msgid "One of the simplest tactics that Deep use to defend their homes is to drop rocks on the threat, which is often grounded and dangerous. This method may be tiring and somewhat ineffective due to the relative precision of the shots, but Deep value their safety enough to employ it often."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Shrieker, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Shrieker.cfg:4
msgid "Shrieker"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Deep Shrieker, race=deep, gender=female
#: Deep/units/Shrieker.cfg:20
msgid ""
"As the moon hides behind the peaks, the wind in the gloom calls.\n"
"Answer it fast! Answer it quick! Quiet shall be your fall.\n"
"To uncover the night's secrets, won't you heed this soft howl?\n"
"Answer it fast, trust the spirits, run with the winds and wolves.\n"
"Won't you come deeper down the forest, in the shadows with us to dance?\n"
"'Til the morrow, the wind shall rest, and wait for you, for its next chance.\n"
"As the moon returns in white flame, it shall be back for your regrets.\n"
"Answer it well, it knows your name, and certainly never forgets."
msgstr ""

